      "kind": "item",
      "label": "I26: the compact drawer opens 0.1s after the pointer rests on it, closes 0.15s after it leaves -- not the 800ms hover delay pop-ups use",
      "excerpt": "I26: the compact drawer opens 0.1s after the pointer rests on it, closes 0.15s after it leaves -- not the 800ms hover delay pop-ups use",
      "text": "Change to a 1/2 second hover to open.  Close timing is fine.\nThe fixed icons (home, person, etc) should not move when the drawer opens -- keep the same left padding in open and closed modes.\n\nExpanded menu should be the entire height of the page to match the collapsed sidebar",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-17T01:38:18.978Z",
      "status": "new",
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-17T01:38:50.527Z"
      },
      "working": "2026-11-17T01:38:50.527Z"
    },
    "c2": {
      "anchor": "j181",
      "kind": "item",
      "label": "I35: only a group of ONE listed page with the group's own name (any case) becomes that page alone (jarvis-new's Home, its dialogs not listed); a one-page group of another name keeps its header, as it ",
      "excerpt": "I35: only a group of ONE listed page with the group's own name (any case) becomes that page alone (jarvis-new's Home, its dialogs not listed); a one-page group of another name keeps its header, as it ",
      "text": "Single page in a group should not have a header, no matter if the names don't match",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-17T01:45:54.623Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-17T01:49:09.588Z",
          "html": "<p>Done:  a group with one page in the drawer is now just that page, whatever the group is called.  The page keeps its own icon, or takes the group's if it has none.  Groups of two or more pages keep their header.</p>\n<p>Committed as 06b6310fa;  it reaches main with the next merge (another agent's work in the worktree is mid-edit).</p>",
          "commit": "06b6310fa"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-17T01:47:52.963Z"
      }
    },
    "c3": {
      "anchor": "j183",
      "kind": "item",
      "label": "I35: a site whose FIRST row is an open group lines up the group's label, not exactly: its label's smaller text and the well's own room leave it a few px off. None does today (jarvis-new starts with Ho",
      "excerpt": "I35: a site whose FIRST row is an open group lines up the group's label, not exactly: its label's smaller text and the well's own room leave it a few px off. None does today (jarvis-new starts with Ho",
      "text": "what are you talking about?",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-17T01:47:11.703Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-17T01:49:17.814Z",
          "html": "<p>Sorry, that one was written from inside the code.  In plain words:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>I35 lines up the drawer's <b>first row</b> with the sidebar button's icon, at the same height.</li>\n<li>If a site's drawer ever started with a <b>group</b> (a header with several pages under it) rather than a single page, that first row would be the group's header, which is 28px tall, not 32px, so its icon would sit about 2px off the button's.</li>\n<li>No site starts that way today, and with your C2 rule a one-page group is now just its page, so it's even less likely.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Nothing you can see is wrong.  If you'd rather not keep the note, approve it and it closes.</p>"
        }
      ],
      "claim": {
        "by": "owenoak",
        "agent": "claude",
        "at": "2026-11-17T01:47:48.806Z"
      }
    }
  },
